# Code ownership mirrors the subsystem table in CONTRACTS.md §5.
#
# A CODEOWNERS entry means "this person's review is required", not "only this
# person may change it". Later rules win, so the most specific rule for a path
# is the one that applies.
#
# Replace the team handles below with real GitHub teams before the repository
# is made public; an entry pointing at a team that does not exist silently
# requests no review at all.

# Fallback: anything not claimed below.
*                                   @avgen-project/maintainers

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Frozen core
# These are the contracts every other subsystem imports. Changes here need the
# core maintainers and, for anything in CONTRACTS.md §3 or §4, an accepted RFC.
/src/avgen/core/                    @avgen-project/core-maintainers
/src/avgen/parallel/                @avgen-project/parallel-maintainers
/src/avgen/simulate/                @avgen-project/parallel-maintainers
/src/avgen/__init__.py              @avgen-project/core-maintainers
/CONTRACTS.md                       @avgen-project/steering
/README.md                          @avgen-project/steering

